hexl
------------------------------------------
Intel HE Acceleration Library is an open-source library which provides
efficient implementations of integer arithmetic on Galois fields. Such
arithmetic is prevalent in cryptography, particularly in homomorphic
encryption (HE) schemes. Intel HE Acceleration Library targets integer
arithmetic with word-sized primes, typically 30-60 bits. Intel HE Acceleration
Library provides an API for 64-bit unsigned integers and targets Intel CPUs.

Runtime requirements:
  cygwin-3.6.11-1
  libcpu_features0-0.11.0-1bl3
  libgcc1-14.4.0-1
  libhexl-devel-1.2.6-1bl1
  libhexl1-1.2.6-1bl1
  libstdc++6-14.4.0-1
  pkg-config-3.0.8-1

Build requirements:
(besides corresponding -devel packages)
  binutils-2.47-1
  cmake-4.4.4-1
  cygport-0.37.10-1
  gcc-core-14.4.0-1
  gcc-g++-14.4.0-1
  libbenchmark-devel-1.9.5-1bl2
  libcpu_features-devel-0.11.0-1bl3
  libgtest-devel-1.18.0-1bl1
  ninja-1.13.2-1

Canonical website:
  https://github.com/IntelLabs/hexl

Canonical download:
  https://github.com/IntelLabs/hexl/archive/refs/tags/v1.2.6.tar.gz

-------------------------------------------

Build instructions:
  1. unpack hexl-1.2.6-X-src.tar.xz
  2. if you use setup to install this src package,
     it will be unpacked under /usr/src automatically
        % cd /usr/src
        % cygport ./hexl-1.2.6-X.cygport all

This will create:
  /usr/src/hexl-1.2.6-X-src.tar.xz
  /usr/src/hexl-1.2.6-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libhexl1-1.2.6-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libhexl-devel-1.2.6-X.tar.xz

